!***************************************************************
!This test is based on the Zel'dovich nitric oxide mechanism
! involving two reactions and its reverse as discussed 
! in Al-Khateeb et al. 2009. The aim of the test is to 
! evaluate the inverse reaction rate coefficients applying 
! the thermodynamic method discussed in Grassi et al. 2013
! and employed in KROME.
! Initial conditions are n = 1e-3 mols, Volume = 1e3 cm3 and
! T = 4000 Kelvin.
!***************************************************************

KROME-X notes:
- output files (legacy name): abundances.dat (fort.66).
- legacy -reverse (a generation flag reversing every reaction) is not a
  KROME-X option: the reverse reactions are declared in the network with
  <->. NO_reverse.knet is networks/NO.knet with both reactions written
  as <-> (what kromex/convert_legacy.py networks/react_NO --reverse
  writes). The reverse rate is k_fwd / K_c, K_c from the NASA
  polynomials of data/thermo_burcat.toml (Burcat's database; for these
  five species the same polynomials as legacy's thermo30.dat).
- the species columns of abundances.dat are in KROME-X (alphabetical) order:
  N N2 NO O O2 (legacy: order of appearance N2 O NO N O2); plot.py picks
  them by name.
- as in legacy, the time written is t + the next (1.5x larger) dt.
- KROME-X and legacy agree to the 3 digits written (the largest difference is
  one unit in the last digit, N at early times).
